 "eventMetadata": {
  "context_description": "The trader consensus reflected in these implied probabilities stems primarily from the San Antonio Spurs’ rapid ascent, capped by their Game 7 victory over the defending-champion Oklahoma City Thunder in the Western Conference finals. Victor Wembanyama’s elite two-way dominance and the team’s defensive efficiency propelled a historic turnaround from back-to-back 22-win seasons to a 62-20 regular-season mark and home-court advantage in the NBA Finals. The New York Knicks counter with an 11-game postseason winning streak and superior offensive spacing featuring Jalen Brunson and Karl-Anthony Towns, yet they face the challenge of overcoming San Antonio’s depth and rest advantage after sweeping their Eastern Conference path. This positioning underscores how the Spurs’ youth, roster construction, and recent playoff resilience shape current market sentiment heading into the series.",
